{
  "name": "Extract YouTube video transcripts with YT to Text API",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Extract YouTube Transcripts via YT to Text API\n\n### How it works\nFetch clean, timestamped YouTube transcripts through the hosted YT to Text REST API without cloud IP blocks or proxy maintenance.\n\n1. **Configure & submit:** Sets your video ID, language, and API key, then queues an idempotent job (`POST /api/v1/transcripts`).\n2. **Poll status:** Waits 5 seconds and checks `statusUrl` until `status` is `completed`.\n3. **Split output:** Splits `results` into one item per video (`videoId`, `title`, `text`, and `segments`) ready for OpenAI, Claude, or Notion.\n\n### Setup steps\n- [ ] Generate a `ytt_live_...` token at [yttotext.com/developers](https://yttotext.com/developers).\n- [ ] Paste your `apiKey`, `videoId`, and `language` into **Set Video & API Key**.\n- [ ] Click **Test workflow** to inspect the returned transcript items.\n\n### Customization\n- **Batch mode:** Add up to 50 video IDs in the `ids` array of **Create Transcript Request**.\n- **Automate:** Swap the manual trigger for a Webhook, RSS, or Schedule node.\n\nDocs: [yttotext.com/youtube-transcript-api](https://yttotext.com/youtube-transcript-api)",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 560
      },
      "id": "sticky-main-overview",
      "name": "Sticky Note — Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -496,
        336
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Configure input & submit job\n\nSets your YouTube video ID, language, and API key, then queues an idempotent transcript extraction request.",
        "height": 304,
